  title: British Singapura
  info: In the 1300s, Singapore was named Temasek by the Malay, meaning 'Sea Town'.
    The story goes that a prince discovered a strange beast said to be a lion, and
    named the settlement Singapura, meaning 'Lion City'. At this time, Singapore's
    population was about 1000, mostly Malays and Chinese. The Malay Archipelago was
    mainly under Dutch control at the time.
